Question Text:
What is the test statistic corresponding to the following hypothesis test?
\begin{eqnarray}
H_0:\; \beta_0 &=& 0 \\
H_1:\; \beta_0 & \ne & 0 
\end{eqnarray}

Explanation:
Suppose that $\hat{Y} = \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 \ln(X_1)$. Then if we double $X' = 2 X_1$,
\begin{eqnarray}
\hat{Y}' &=& \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 \ln(X') \\ 
&=& \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 \ln(2 X) \\  
&=& \hat{\beta}_0 + \hat{\beta}_1 (\ln(2) + \ln(X)) \\  
&=& \hat{\beta}_1 \ln(2) + \hat{Y}
\end{eqnarray}
